  "response_text": "Changing the program counter as was done in the lab essentially tells the OS directly where it will be reading instructions. As a result, the PC jumps directly to where the machine code for the print_continuously function in memory.\\nThis leads to the print_continously function being immediately executed without the , since the PC registers dictates what instruction in the code the CPU is executing.\\nThink of it like reaching a superscript footnote when reading a book. Even though there are words after the footnote marker, many readers will instead jump to the text of the footnote immediately.\\n",
